data: {"index":0,"delta":{"content":{"text":"**Calculating Set Cardinalities**\n\nI've determined the cardinalities of sets A and B, representing integers divisible by 7 and 11, respectively, up to 999.  I have also computed the cardinality of their intersection, the set of integers divisible by both 7 and 11. Specifically, I found |A| = 142, |B| = 90, and |A ∩ B| = 12. Using these values, I've calculated the symmetric difference: |A △ B| = |A| + |B| - 2|A ∩ B|. This gives a final answer of 218.\n\n\n","type":"text"},"type":"thought_summary"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

